  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Train-the-trainer programme on combat trauma and PTSD Tunisia 2016</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Train-the-trainer (TTT) programme on combat trauma and post traumatic stress syndrome (PTSD) to strengthen the (para-)military mental health organisation in Tunisia.The objective of the TTT programme in 2016 is threefold.&#x2022;	Capacity building of TUN security forces:The aim is to contribute in the field of security, in the form of expertise and knowledge transfer for dealing with Combat Trauma Posttraumatic Stress Syndrome. &#x2022;	Support:There are concerns about the deteriorating security situation - growing influence of extremist Salafists, large number of jihad travellers to Syria, increasing illegal arms imports from Libya, ongoing skirmishes with terrorist groups near the border with Algeria and poorly functioning security apparatus.&#x2022;	Closure:The 2016 programme will conclude the TTT programme, which started in Tunisia in 2013. By providing one more annual programme, the transfer of knowledge and expertise, which took place over the past years, will be monitored and secured for the future.</narrative>
  </description>
